# Secure files

{{projectName}} was generated with the `secure_files` capability. A stored
file's bytes are exposed only after they were hashed, scanned and released
clean; nothing here can be switched off by a setting. The Starter's
`docs/SECURE_FILES.md` is the full reference; this page is what an operator of
this product needs.

## It refuses to start without

The API and the worker both refuse to start, naming every missing setting, unless
all of these are present and valid. There is no fallback to unscanned release.

| Setting | Requirement |
|---------|-------------|
| `FILE_SCAN_BACKEND` | a real scanner (`clamd`), never `none` |
| `FILE_SCAN_CLAMD_HOST` | set |
| `FILE_SCAN_CLAMD_PORT` | a port, 1-65535 |
| `STORAGE_ENDPOINT` | set |
| `STORAGE_BUCKET` | set |
| `STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY` | set |
| `STORAGE_SECRET_KEY` | set |
| `REDIS_URL` | set: a confirmed upload is finalized by a job |
| `DATABASE_URL` | set: the finalizer works on the file's row, as its tenant |

Later releases of the capability add rows; the list lives in
`services/api/koras_api/core/secure_files.py` (`SECURE_FILES_CHECKS`).

## Uploads

A ticket is issued only for a SHA-256 claim (`checksum_sha256`, 64 lowercase hex
characters, required), and it lets the browser write one *incoming* key and nothing
else. The worker's `file.finalize` job copies the object to a *final* key only it can
write, after checking the object's provenance and the digest of both the incoming and
the final bytes against the claim. Until that has happened the file is on a key a client
could still write, is not downloadable, and is not handed to anything.

If a file stays unavailable: check the worker is running and can reach `REDIS_URL`,
`DATABASE_URL` and the bucket; the sweep (`sweep_finalize`, every five minutes) picks up
anything a lost job left. A file the finalizer refused carries a `scan_failure` word and a
`storage.upload.held` audit event; `integrity_mismatch` means the bytes were not the ones
claimed and is never retried. The bucket's CORS rule must allow the signed upload headers
(see the Starter's `docs/SECURE_FILES.md`).

## Changing the mode

`secure_files` is a generation-time choice. It is not a runtime toggle and is not
retrofitted by upgrading the Starter. Do not hand-edit it in or out: regenerate,
or extend the profile manifest in `koras-saas-starter`.
